      "content": "Thanks, that makes sense. The problem is that I can't really run Valgrind or heavy sanitizers on this hardware—the overhead is just too high for the ECU to even boot, let alone run the actual application logic.\n\nIt's feeling extremely elusive. The memory consumption increments so slowly that it's hard to tell if it's a true leak or just fragmentation, and there's no obvious pattern in the logs. It's like the memory just... disappears into a black hole every few minutes.\n\nSince I can't use heavy profiling tools, what are some low-level, manual ways I can track these allocations? I'm looking for something more surgical that I can implement directly in the firmware without blowing the timing budget.",
